//- The policy screen. Six checkboxes with the same shape, and the roles they
//- describe are the four the server stores.

mixin policyToggle(id, label)
  label.field.checkbox-field
    input(id=id, type='checkbox')
    | #{label}

button#adminSettingsBack.button.ghost(type='button') ← Back to workflow
h1 Flyer Studio settings
p Settings apply to new configurations and IGSNs. Existing files keep their location and permissions.

h2 Shared workspace
label.field
  | Collection
  select#workspaceCollection
button#browseWorkspaceBtn.button.ghost(type='button') Choose workspace folder
label.field
  | Workspace path
  input#workspacePath(placeholder='/collection/Flyer Studio/Workspace')
p.field-note Choose a folder inside a collection. Collaborators also need access to that destination; the settings below do not change the collection’s permissions.

h2 Users and groups
label.field
  | Find a user or group
  input#principalSearch(placeholder='Search by name')
button#findPrincipalsBtn.button.ghost(type='button') Search
label.field
  | Results
  select#principalResults
label.field
  | Add to
  select#principalRole
    option(value='creators') IGSN creators
    option(value='owners') Owners
    option(value='editors') Editors
    option(value='viewers') Viewers
button#addPrincipalBtn.button.ghost(type='button') Add user or group
#policyLists
p.field-note Creators are attribution only. Groups appear as organizational creators. Owners can manage access; editors can modify data; viewers can read. The highest matching access level wins.

h2 Acting user
+policyToggle('creators_include_user', 'Include the registrant as an IGSN creator')
+policyToggle('owners_include_user', 'Include the acting user as an owner')
+policyToggle('editors_include_user', 'Include the acting user as an editor')
+policyToggle('viewers_include_user', 'Include the acting user as a viewer')

h2 Visibility
+policyToggle('public_igsn', 'Make new stack IGSNs public')
+policyToggle('public_files', 'Make new configuration folders and files public')
p.field-note IGSN access uses the same owners, editors, and viewers. Parent foil permissions remain unchanged.

button#saveAdminSettingsBtn.button.primary(type='button') Save settings
p#settingsStatus(role='status')
